`switch_dist_1_1` is missing the `network 10.1.1.0/24 area 0.0.0.1` statement. It never originates a Type-1 LSA for the pod-1 host subnet, so no other router in the OSPF domain learns a path back to 10.1.1.0/24. This is confirmed by the "Destination Net Unreachable" ICMP from switch_dist_2_1 — it has no FIB entry for 10.1.1.0/24. The switch_dist_1_1 eth0 uplink IS in OSPF (hence switch_dist_1_1 itself can forward outbound traffic and ping the server farm), but return packets are dropped by every router that lacks the missing route.

